.TH FOREST-SCREENSHOT 1 "October 2026" "forest" "Forest desktop environment"
.SH NAME
forest-screenshot \- take a screenshot in the Forest desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B forest-screenshot
.RB [ \-\-region ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B forest-screenshot
captures all outputs, or with
.B \-\-region
an area selected with
.BR slurp (1),
using
.BR grim (1).
The image is saved to
.I Screenshots
under the XDG pictures directory, copied to the clipboard, and announced
with a desktop notification. It is bound to Meta+S and Ctrl+Meta+S by
default.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR forest (1),
.BR grim (1),
.BR slurp (1)
